{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"jarl/tests/proof_cases/storage_view.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T08:27:44.591516Z","id":"7c8beafc9720b6a0c6f3f31cf5df0b8e69c84829a7eb1f5f7bbe072e0aade388","body":{"detail":"Only the `.saturating_sub(1)` mutation has kernel=true (line 40). The mutations `filter(|_| !snapshot_changed)` and `truncate_from: None` (lines 41-46) skip the `Lean rejected Proofs.lean` check (lines 52-54). The `.rev()` mutation of Write::entries (lines 60-70) asserts only `is_err()`. All three pass if the frontend rejects the shape, the copied crate fails to build, or Lean runs out of memory. README.md:91-92 says 'Source mutations must fail in the invariant proof, not just the parser or Rust compiler', and PROGRESS.md (Cargo provenance section, near line 1397) concedes that 'unsupported storage-view shapes remain frontend rejections'. As a result, the snapshot-changed filter, the truncate_from field binding and the iteration order of Write::entries have no negative control that reaches the theorems exact_view, entries_exact or source_checkpoint.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":39},"end":{"line":70},"content_hash":"7ef8e56baaa2dbefcdeaa6b6c588ff7a6365e584cc0563bd552e5b293d36830c"},"suggested_fix":"Pick mutations of these three properties that the frontend accepts (for example `filter(|_| snapshot_changed && false)`, or `truncate_from: from.map(|i| i + 1)`), and require `Lean rejected Proofs.lean` for each. If no such mutation exists, narrow README.md:91-92 to name the storage-view mutations that are only frontend rejections.","summary":"Three of the four storage-view source mutations accept any error, so they can pass on a frontend or Cargo failure instead of a proof failure","tags":["review","review:2026-10-07-deep","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"jarl/tests/proof_cases/replication_contract.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T08:27:44.591567Z","id":"a9fddc42ac758af2dced37cf03b3ebace72594abfa453455f3d19010442a99f5","body":{"detail":"Line 53 asserts only `error.contains(\"Lean rejected\")`. Every other Jarl negative control requires `Lean rejected Proofs.lean`. replication-contract imports ../storage/Proofs.lean and ../message-validation/Proofs.lean as proof_modules (jarl/proofs/replication-contract/project.json). Both mutations (`checked_sub(1)?` in State::get and `self.last().index >= from` in State::truncate) are already covered by the imported storage/log-boundary contracts, so the error is likely `Lean rejected StorageContracts.lean`, or a Generated.lean failure, before Replication.* is elaborated. README.md:229-230 says the project's '32-bit check rejects source mutations to the lookup offset and truncation boundary', which suggests that Replication.lookup_identifies_predecessor and matched_replacement_preserves_log are what reject them.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":46},"end":{"line":55},"content_hash":"c8afefc69e0a95814af542890a7182f621344e571fa2d3cd0ca5efa8739c045e"},"suggested_fix":"Assert the specific file that must reject each mutation. If the intent is that the composition is sensitive, add a mutation that only the Replication theorems constrain, such as changing the `truncate(entry.id.index)` boundary inside Node::append, and require `Lean rejected Proofs.lean`. Otherwise reword README.md:229-230 to say the imported storage contracts reject these mutations.","summary":"The replication mutation check accepts a rejection of any Lean file, so it never shows that the replication theorems themselves catch the mutation","tags":["review","review:2026-10-07-deep","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"jarl/tests/proof_cases/lean.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T08:27:44.591613Z","id":"ecd5f2eab79c6bac7fd21a92caec2274ea6bb8ebd2f3de58d10c1f25fb440571","body":{"detail":"jarl/tests/proof_cases/lean.rs:29-61 builds a new fixture for each mutation: it flattens slice source paths to bare file names and copies Proofs.lean. It checks only that verification fails with `Lean rejected Proofs.lean`. The same fixture configuration is never verified unmutated. jarl/tests/proof_cases/methods.rs:5-39 and queries.rs:37-79 (each_missing_input_gate_breaks_the_original_source_contract) have the same shape. Any failure common to the fixture would therefore count as a successful negative control: a Proofs.lean that no longer elaborates with flattened sources, a missing import, a heartbeat limit, or Lean hitting the `--memory` cap that provium/src/project.rs:415-447 sets from PROVIUM_LEAN_MEMORY_MB. All of these produce `Lean rejected Proofs.lean`. scalar_methods.rs:100 and arrays.rs:176 do verify the unmutated fixture first, and they show the intended pattern.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":4},"end":{"line":63},"content_hash":"af9c68410296724d5471715120520424df284ef938277c3b4cb397836d114628"},"suggested_fix":"In lean.rs, methods.rs and queries.rs, run `verify(...).unwrap()` on the unmutated fixture, built the same way as the mutated ones, before applying the mutations. Also check that the Lean error text is not a resource-exhaustion message such as 'maximum heartbeats' or 'memory'.","summary":"The consensus, persistence and input-gating negative controls never verify their unmutated fixture, so a fixture-level Lean failure satisfies them","tags":["review","review:2026-10-07-deep","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"jarl/tests/proof_cases/arrays.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T08:27:44.592121Z","id":"32addfd94e1306a5be1b416c6317414d98ca5040311c929eb82bc38bc6d7ba52","body":{"detail":"The 23 mutations cover the rank divisor, the old_voters loop and the quorum threshold. They do not touch `new.min(old)` (src/membership.rs:163) or `if !self.is_joint() { return new; }` (src/membership.rs:153-155), although QuorumIndex.execution fixes both. Only the separate consensus slice test (jarl/tests/proof_cases/lean.rs:16) mutates `new.min(old)`, and that runs against the scalar slice project, not the complete membership method translation.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":180},"end":{"line":215},"content_hash":"1bd68b631eb50fc4279473ca5b869b2c17a17552e39840332f3250a13f946d74"},"suggested_fix":"Add (\"new.min(old)\", \"new.max(old)\") and (\"if !self.is_joint() {\", \"if self.is_joint() {\") to the arrays.rs mutation list, each required to fail with 'Lean rejected Proofs.lean'.","summary":"The membership mutation suite never mutates quorum_index's final minimum or its stable early return","tags":["review","review:2026-10-07-deep","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"jarl/tests/proof_cases/storage_view.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T10:08:39.037791Z","id":"6578e0361c19ae106e909c59a0fbfce5381742a7764f08a640ab752ed8b259dc","body":{"detail":"storage_view.rs:39-47: only (\".saturating_sub(1)\", ..., true) sets kernel=true. The 'filter(|_| snapshot_changed)' and 'truncate_from: from,' mutations set kernel=false, so the 'Lean rejected Proofs.lean' assertion at :52-54 is skipped and only unwrap_err() at :51 applies. The ready.rs '.rev()' mutation at :60-70 asserts only verify(...).is_err(). README.md:91-92 says 'Source mutations must fail in the invariant proof, not just the parser or Rust compiler'. PROGRESS.md:1400 concedes that 'unsupported storage-view shapes remain frontend' rejections.","kind":"comment","references":"7c8beafc9720b6a0c6f3f31cf5df0b8e69c84829a7eb1f5f7bbe072e0aade388","summary":"confirmed: only the saturating_sub mutation must reach Lean; the filter, truncate_from and .rev() mutations accept any error","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"jarl/tests/proof_cases/replication_contract.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T10:08:39.037807Z","id":"707e7a30eb0c030ca0cc788842846bc2664652d208448fd5751cf31067b230bb","body":{"detail":"replication_contract.rs:53 asserts only error.contains(\"Lean rejected\"). provium/src/methods.rs:1379-1389 checks Generated.lean, then each proof_modules library, then Proofs.lean. provium/src/project.rs:447 formats the error as 'Lean rejected {file}'. jarl/proofs/replication-contract/project.json imports ../storage/Proofs.lean as StorageContracts, and that file references state_State_truncate 48 times, so the truncate-boundary mutation (src/state.rs:161) can be rejected by StorageContracts before any Replication.* theorem is checked. README.md:229-230 credits the project's own 32-bit check with rejecting these mutations. One minor inaccuracy: not every other negative control requires 'Lean rejected Proofs.lean' (storage_view.rs:52 sets kernel=false), but that does not affect the claim.","kind":"comment","references":"a9fddc42ac758af2dced37cf03b3ebace72594abfa453455f3d19010442a99f5","summary":"confirmed: the mutation check accepts any 'Lean rejected' file, and the imported StorageContracts module is elaborated before Proofs.lean","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"jarl/tests/proof_cases/lean.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T10:08:39.037820Z","id":"8ccd4baf0dc13b8c1953728b282944bd0564cc03d3a7709d8dfb75fbd846e378","body":{"detail":"lean.rs:29-61 builds a new Work for each mutation, flattens slice sources to bare file names (:40-48), copies Proofs.lean, and asserts only unwrap_err plus 'Lean rejected Proofs.lean'. No unmutated flattened fixture is verified; the 32-bit test at :67-87 uses canonical paths instead. methods.rs:5-39 mutates ready.rs before its only verify call. queries.rs each_missing_input_gate_breaks_the_original_source_contract mutates node.rs before its only verify call. provium/src/project.rs:413-447 runs Lean with --memory and maps any nonzero exit to 'Lean rejected {file}', so resource exhaustion gives the same text. By contrast, arrays.rs:177 and scalar_methods.rs:101 call verify(...).unwrap() on the fixture before mutating it.","kind":"comment","references":"ecd5f2eab79c6bac7fd21a92caec2274ea6bb8ebd2f3de58d10c1f25fb440571","summary":"confirmed: lean.rs, methods.rs and the queries.rs gating test never verify their unmutated fixture before asserting 'Lean rejected Proofs.lean'","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"jarl/tests/proof_cases/arrays.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T10:08:39.037899Z","id":"f5f59ae06a151679a035110417a26e974f2ac147f557f56a5a940dbe100372bb","body":{"detail":"arrays.rs:180-213 lists 23 (from, to) pairs. They include 'count / 2 + 1', the old_voters loop and 'count > total / 2', but not 'new.min(old)' (src/membership.rs:163) or 'if !self.is_joint() {' (src/membership.rs:153). QuorumIndex.execution (membership/Proofs.lean:1406-1417) fixes both, with min first second and the is_joint branch. Only lean.rs:16 mutates new.min(old), and it runs against the consensus slice project.","kind":"comment","references":"32addfd94e1306a5be1b416c6317414d98ca5040311c929eb82bc38bc6d7ba52","summary":"confirmed: none of the 23 membership mutations touches new.min(old) or the !self.is_joint() early return","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"jarl/tests/proof_cases/arrays.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T14:31:29.697016Z","id":"1fb0c124269e3c22e30cd98bc76ad695bfb6936cdce6105950237da2a715ed76","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:3930f70d722cec6728c49f4c2c906982bedcb057","summary":"The membership mutation suite now mutates quorum_index's final minimum and stable early return; the numeric-fold frontend rejects both shapes, and the test asserts each specific rejection ('expected builtin lookup min', 'numeric early return needs negated source query'); the semantic content is pinned by QuorumIndex.result_majority. original_membership_mutations_break_the_array_contracts passed.","supersedes":"32addfd94e1306a5be1b416c6317414d98ca5040311c929eb82bc38bc6d7ba52","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"jarl/tests/proof_cases/lean.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T14:31:29.697092Z","id":"bdefb873aaa49d0320ec0b3db49789e135d64867fb029cda5c29327f4f07f346","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:3930f70d722cec6728c49f4c2c906982bedcb057","summary":"lean.rs (consensus), methods.rs (persistence) and queries.rs (input gating) now verify the unmutated fixture successfully before any mutation; all three passed in the full Jarl gate.","supersedes":"ecd5f2eab79c6bac7fd21a92caec2274ea6bb8ebd2f3de58d10c1f25fb440571","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"jarl/tests/proof_cases/replication_contract.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T14:31:29.697158Z","id":"2006dd374be561798147ba4c0cbc126de2e938f9fb35a50e188694813cd11aeb","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:3930f70d722cec6728c49f4c2c906982bedcb057","summary":"The replication mutation check now requires the rejection to come from Proofs.lean or the imported StorageContracts.lean, never generated code or the Provium library. Isolating Proofs.lean alone is not possible, since it builds on storage lemmas about the same functions; the test comment records this. composed_replacement_verifies_on_32_bit_and_rejects_changed_lookup_and_cut passed.","supersedes":"a9fddc42ac758af2dced37cf03b3ebace72594abfa453455f3d19010442a99f5","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"jarl/tests/proof_cases/storage_view.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T14:31:29.697228Z","id":"85d4d662b1530a79612d053a2ae56e997bb79713cac25d08f3d879cd051b9118","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:3930f70d722cec6728c49f4c2c906982bedcb057","summary":"Each storage-view mutation now asserts its specific outcome: saturating_sub reaches Lean; the snapshot filter, truncate_from and reversed-entries mutations assert the frontend's named rejections ('view filter must test its boolean input', 'unsupported shared view field expression', 'expected builtin lookup flatten'). delta_contracts_reject_source_and_host_order_changes passed.","supersedes":"7c8beafc9720b6a0c6f3f31cf5df0b8e69c84829a7eb1f5f7bbe072e0aade388","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
